  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Durable deadlines can now live in Quartz.NET.\n\n**New package**\n-  — , an  over a Quartz.NET scheduler. A deployment already running Quartz with a persistent job store keeps each waiting instance's wake in those tables. Depends on the  core alone, so it serves any runtime.\n\n\n\n**Changes**\n- :  resolves a deadline scheduler from DI and runs the journal projection with it, in place of the built-in bucket entities.\n- One Quartz job per deadline, one trigger per arm. A disarm deletes the job; a wake reschedules its own trigger before waking, so a consumed deadline stays gone and a wake racing a re-arm stands down.\n- Retries back off (30s doubling, capped at 10m) for up to  (default 10, ~55 minutes), then the job is deleted with an error log and the instance fires its deadline the next time something activates it (guarantee ).\n-  holds its deadlines in a clustered Quartz store in the same Postgres database as the journal.\n\n**Note:**  and  both define . A file importing both namespaces needs an alias, e.g. .\n\nSee [](https://github.com/yanpitangui/sagant/blob/main/docs/deadlines-and-scheduling.md#holding-deadlines-in-quartznet--sagantschedulingquartz).",
